1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,130
On this IC Command Board, the training
warehouse call is already open.

2
00:00:04,619 --> 00:00:08,319
Select Tactical Maps to review additional
maps for this incident.

3
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:12,250
The count is zero, and the empty state
explains that a map can

4
00:00:12,250 --> 00:00:14,260
represent an area of operation.

5
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:18,250
Choose Add in this section to begin a
named reference map.

6
00:00:18,459 --> 00:00:22,249
New Tactical Map provides Name,
Description and Expires.

7
00:00:22,689 --> 00:00:25,559
Before a name is entered, Add is
unavailable.

8
00:00:26,070 --> 00:00:32,280
Read the expiry choices: None, twelve
hours, one day, two days or seven days.

9
00:00:32,710 --> 00:00:36,389
Decide what the map should identify and
how long that reference should remain

10
00:00:36,389 --> 00:00:38,090
relevant to your department’s work.

11
00:00:38,269 --> 00:00:41,009
Enter a name that another operator can
recognize.

12
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:44,540
Here it is Training Only, West gate
coordination.

13
00:00:44,979 --> 00:00:48,200
The Description explains that this is a
fictional reference area

14
00:00:48,229 --> 00:00:49,630
for the training staging lane.

15
00:00:50,059 --> 00:00:54,639
The twelve-hour choice has been selected,
and the form displays a calculated expiry.

16
00:00:55,049 --> 00:00:58,850
Review the entered description and
displayed time before choosing Add.

17
00:00:59,039 --> 00:01:02,099
The board now shows Tactical Maps with a
count of one.

18
00:01:02,559 --> 00:01:06,869
The card contains the saved name,
description and an Expires label.

19
00:01:07,359 --> 00:01:11,510
Compare that readback with the prepared
form: this recording shows different

20
00:01:11,510 --> 00:01:13,170
clock times in those two views.

21
00:01:13,579 --> 00:01:17,499
Verify the intended expiry in your
department before relying on it.

22
00:01:17,970 --> 00:01:21,330
The named card gives the next operator a
clear purpose to check

23
00:01:21,439 --> 00:01:22,830
when opening this reference.

24
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:26,309
Use the pencil button on the Staging lane
to open its settings,

25
00:01:26,630 --> 00:01:28,800
then scroll to Attached Map.

26
00:01:29,300 --> 00:01:32,739
None and the named West gate coordination
map are available.

27
00:01:33,189 --> 00:01:36,869
Select the intended map and check the
selected state before saving.

28
00:01:37,189 --> 00:01:40,080
This associates that reference with the
lane you are editing.

29
00:01:40,460 --> 00:01:43,769
Keep the lane identity and the map’s name
clear when several

30
00:01:43,769 --> 00:01:45,259
areas are being coordinated.

31
00:01:45,479 --> 00:01:47,640
Choose Save in the lane settings.

32
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:53,130
After a fresh page load, reopen the same
Staging lane and return to Attached Map.

33
00:01:53,519 --> 00:01:55,599
The named map remains selected here.

34
00:01:55,969 --> 00:01:58,540
This readback confirms the saved
association.

35
00:01:59,009 --> 00:02:02,499
Check the selected map whenever a lane’s
purpose or working area

36
00:02:02,499 --> 00:02:06,120
changes, so the next operator can find the
intended reference.

37
00:02:06,269 --> 00:02:08,259
Return to Tactical Maps on the board.

38
00:02:08,779 --> 00:02:13,310
The count of one, the saved name,
Description and Expires label are still

39
00:02:13,310 --> 00:02:15,260
present after the fresh navigation.

40
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:17,319
Read the card before opening it.

41
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:21,700
A short, specific description helps
distinguish a staging reference from

42
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:26,469
another team’s search area, patrol sector
or industrial exercise location.

43
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:28,810
Open the card and check the map’s header.

44
00:02:29,209 --> 00:02:33,279
It shows the same West gate coordination
name, with the training street map and

45
00:02:33,279 --> 00:02:35,610
Squad Three’s Search Division label below.

46
00:02:36,079 --> 00:02:39,640
Use that identity check when sharing
references with another operator.

47
00:02:40,169 --> 00:02:43,650
Named areas can support community
paramedicine or mental health

48
00:02:43,650 --> 00:02:47,779
coordination, search and rescue, security
companies, wildland

49
00:02:47,779 --> 00:02:52,570
contractors, industrial response teams,
and fire or EMS departments.

50
00:02:53,039 --> 00:02:56,369
Choose names and descriptions that explain
your own team’s work.

